{
  "skill_name": "worlddriver-rpc",
  "description": "Call the worlddriver Minecraft mod's live control API over its JSON-RPC websocket (port 39801) with the bundled rpc.py client, and look up exact method params in its complete 45-method reference. Use this skill whenever you need to DRIVE or QUERY a running worlddriver client/bot \u2014 calling mc.bot.* (goto, setting, mine, build, status, cancel), mc.action.* (runCommand, fill, placeMany), mc.observe.*, mc.client.* (input, screenshot, screen, chat), mc.query, mc.wait.*, or mc.script.eval. Reach for it ESPECIALLY when the mcp__worlddriver__* tools can't do the job: a setting or param won't apply / gets stripped after you rebuilt the mod (the harness freezes MCP tool schemas at session start, so newly-added keys must be set over RPC instead), you want to send a raw method+params straight to the websocket, you need to script a multi-step live setup (give\u2192tp\u2192fill\u2192setting\u2192goto) in one shell block, or you're bringing the client up headless (title\u2192world, input, screenshots). Also use it to answer \"what RPC methods exist / how do I call X\" for this mod. This is for INVOKING the mod at runtime \u2014 not for editing the mod's Java (BotConfig/ToolCatalog/Walker), writing gametests, or standing up your own MCP server, which are ordinary code tasks. If a task means controlling the live bot/client or bypassing a stale MCP tool, consult this skill rather than guessing the wire format.",
